# LangChain & LlamaIndex

Notebook: [Langchain_llamaindex.ipynb](Langchain_llamaindex.ipynb)

## What I built
- **LangChain chain** – prompt template → Gemini → text (a property listing writer)
- **LangChain agent** – an agent with a rental yield calculator tool
- **LlamaIndex RAG** – asked questions about a lease in a few lines of code

## By hand vs framework
| | By hand (my Lease Reader) | LlamaIndex |
|---|---|---|
| Code | ~50 lines | ~5 lines |
| Control | Full | Less |

## Key learning
Frameworks are faster for prototypes; plain code gives more control. Because I built RAG and agents by hand first, I understand what the frameworks do underneath.
